#' @title Add supplemental qualifiers
#' @description
#' Adds values from a supplemental qualifier (SUPP--) data set as columns, one column for each QNAM.
#'
#' @param domain `character` Name of the domain that gets the new columns
#' @param source `character` Name of the SUPP-- data set, for example SUPPAE
#' @param qnam `character` One or more QNAM values to add as columns
#' @param idvar `character` Name of the variable in `domain` that IDVAR refers to, for example AESEQ. Use NULL for
#' subject-level records, where IDVAR is blank. Do not use "".
#' @type column
#' @origin Predecessor
#' @depends {{{domain}}} USUBJID
{{#idvar}}
#' @depends {{{domain}}} {{{idvar}}}
{{/idvar}}
#' @depends {{{source}}} USUBJID
{{#idvar}}
#' @depends {{{source}}} IDVARVAL
{{/idvar}}
#' @depends {{{source}}} QNAM
#' @depends {{{source}}} QVAL
{{#qnam}}
#' @outputs {{{.}}}
{{/qnam}}
#' @spec Derivation: For each QNAM in `qnam`, make a column with the same name. Copy QVAL from the `source`
#'   record with the same QNAM and the same USUBJID.
#'   When `idvar` is given, the record must also match on the `domain` variable that `idvar` names. When that
#'   variable is numeric, IDVARVAL read as a number is equal to it. When that variable is character, IDVARVAL is the
#'   same text.
#'   When `idvar` is NULL, the match uses only USUBJID, so each record of the subject gets the value.
#'   One `source` record can match more than one `domain` record. Each of these records gets the value.
#'   When no `source` record matches, the value is missing. This includes a `domain` record with a missing
#'   value in the `idvar` variable, a QNAM with no records, and a `source` with zero rows. QNAM must be the same
#'   text. QVAL is copied without change.
#'   Requires: For each `source` record with QNAM in `qnam`:
#'   When `idvar` is given, IDVAR is equal to `idvar`, and IDVARVAL is character and not blank. The `idvar`
#'   variable in `domain` is numeric or character. When it is numeric, IDVARVAL is a number written as text.
#'   When `idvar` is NULL, IDVAR and IDVARVAL are blank ("" or missing).
#'   There is at most one record for each USUBJID, IDVARVAL and QNAM. When the `idvar` variable is numeric, this
#'   applies after IDVARVAL is read as a number.
#'   QVAL is not blank. USUBJID, QNAM and QVAL are character. USUBJID identifies one subject across all studies in
#'   the data.
#'   Guarantees: Each column in `qnam` exists and is character. Its values are QVAL or missing.
